            <ArticleTitle>Effect of isometric handgrip on systolic time intervals in patients with ischemic heart disease and cyclic amp phosphodiesterase inhibitor pretreatment.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>346-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The effect of cAMP phosphodiesterase inhibitor EG626 on the left ventricular function was studied in 23 patients with ischemic heart disease at rest and during the IHG test. Administration of a single dose of the substance produced changes in STIs indicating an increase in cardiac output and a possible enhancement of myocardial contractility during the IHG test. EG626 may have a beneficial effect on impaired left ventricular function in patients with ischemic heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
